<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    SL_LairRoom_DraincasketRoom: a small grim room of Vanilla Races Expanded - Sanguophage
    draincaskets around the hemogen vat that feeds the lair's pipe network. Layout and
    rationale in Source/1.6/MapGen/Rooms/LairRoomWorker_DraincasketRoom.cs; the network in
    Source/1.6/MapGen/Utilities/LairHemogenNet.cs.

    The def itself needs no gate: it references nothing from VRE (the worker reaches VRE's
    defs through SL_HemogenNetDefOf, null without the mod), and the program line that asks
    for it in 1.6/Defs/LairLayoutDefs/SL_Lair.xml carries the MayRequire.

    Rect only, 7 to 9 each way: two caskets a side plus the vat and tap need 7 by 7, and the
    room is meant to feel cramped. Flagstone, as a working room. A dead end (no children, no
    loop doors), so no door opens into the far wall the vat stands against or into a side
    wall's row of caskets.
  -->

  <SanguophageLords.LairRoomDef>
    <defName>SL_LairRoom_DraincasketRoom</defName>
    <workerClass>SanguophageLords.LairRoomWorker_DraincasketRoom</workerClass>
    <floor>Flagstone</floor>
    <corridorChance>0.3</corridorChance>
    <maxChildren>0</maxChildren>
    <allowLoops>false</allowLoops>
    <shapes>
      <li>
        <kind>Rect</kind>
        <across>7~9</across>
        <deep>7~9</deep>
      </li>
    </shapes>
  </SanguophageLords.LairRoomDef>

</Defs>
